raw_content:
Main code compiles. Now write tests. Three test classes:

1. StrataAndCollectApiTest — MockMvc, @MockitoBean Clock, db test_collect.
2. PackageFlowApiTest — MockMvc, db test_package.
3. ConcurrencyBoundaryTest — service-level, db test_conc.

Each with @BeforeEach cleanup deleting all rows (order: package_item, seal_event, request_log, sample, seal_package, stratum).

Test 1 details:
- register stratum → 201, jsonPath id/siteCode.
- duplicate → 409 STRATUM_EXISTS.
- collect with fixed clock: mock clock.instant() → fixed. POST /api/samples → 201, collectedAt == "2026-02-01T00:00:00Z"? Jackson serializes Instant with jackson.time-zone Asia/Shanghai... For Instant, jackson writes ISO-8601 with 'Z' regardless of timezone? InstantSerializer uses ISO-8601 with Z when WRITE_DATES_AS_TIMESTAMPS disabled — actually Instant.toString() → always Z. Time-zone affects LocalDateTime etc., Instant serialized as Instant.toString() → Z. Good, assert endsWith Z value.
- duplicate sampleNo → 409 SAMPLE_EXISTS.
- replay: same requestId same body → 201, same body (compare response content strings equal), and sample count == 1.
- same requestId different sampleNo → 409 IDEMPOTENCY_CONFLICT.
- unknown stratum → 422.
- validation: missing requestId → 400.
- GET query: /api/samples/{no} → stratumNo, gridRef, status COLLECTED, packageNo null.
- GET unknown → 404.

Note: cleanup in @BeforeEach deletes request_log too, so requestIds unique per test anyway.

Mock clock: @MockitoBean Clock clock — but TimeConfig defines clock bean; MockitoBean replaces it. when(clock.instant()).thenReturn(fixed). Also clock.getZone()? Not used. But careful: IdempotencyService uses Instant.now(clock) too — fine.

Actually with @MockitoBean, Mockito mock of abstract class Clock — mock() works.

Test 2 details (PackageFlowApiTest):
- @BeforeEach: clean tables; register stratum L (site SITE-T, stratum L) and L2 via service or MockMvc. Use services autowired for setup brevity, MockMvc for assertions of status codes.
- test twentyItemsHandoverOk:
  - collect 20 samples (service.collect with unique requestIds — note collect is idempotency-wrapped; use distinct requestIds).
  - create package via POST /api/packages → 201, packageNo.
  - add 20 items via POST items → 200 each (addItem returns 200 default). 
